<title>USA: Furniture Brands sells 10 million shares.</title>
<headline>Furniture Brands sells 10 million shares.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Furniture Brands International Inc said Tuesday its secondary offer of 10 million common shares owned by two investor groups was completed at a price of $12.75 per share.</p>
<p>The stock was sold by Apollo Investment Fund and Lion Advisors, which retained all of the proceeds.</p>
<p>Furniture Brands is the parent of Broyhill, Lane and Thomasville, which make home furnishings.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
